<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <base href="/" />
    <ResourcePreloader />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["_content/Norse.Hosting.Web.Components/app.css"]" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["Norse.Hosting.Web.Server.styles.css"]" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="_content/Norse.DesignSystem.Tokens/norse-design-tokens.css" />
    <ImportMap />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/x-icon" href="@Assets["_content/Norse.Hosting.Web.Components/favicon.ico"]" />
    <HeadOutlet @rendermode="PageRenderMode" />
</head>

<body>
    @*
        So rendermode is a hosting level concern which means it doesn't work in MAUI at all ergo default to InteractiveAuto at the top level and then let any routable component with a @page directive override it to InteractiveServer if it wants to.
        This is the only way to get a MAUI app to work with routable components that are prerendered on the server.
        PageRenderMode is null for requests that don't support interactive routing (e.g. direct API/non-navigation
        requests), so those stay static instead of forcing an interactive render mode on them.
    *@
    <NorseFluentDesignTheme />
    <Routes @rendermode="PageRenderMode" />
    <ReconnectModal/>
    <script src="@Assets["_framework/blazor.web.js"]"></script>
    <script src="@Assets["Components/Shared/PasskeySubmit.razor.js"]" type="module"></script>
</body>

</html>

@code {
    [CascadingParameter]
    HttpContext HttpContext { get; set; } = null!;

    @*
        /Account/* pins to InteractiveServer, not Auto: Heimdall's identity components never declare a
        render mode (the host chooses — that's the contract), and the WASM half of Auto cannot run them
        yet — the server never serializes auth state to the client, and the generated gRPC-Web client
        does not dispatch from the WASM renderer (both tracked for feature/hosting-web-server-authn).
        Auto's day-two behavior (cached runtime → WASM) turned every identity page silently inert.
        Himinbjörg's scaffold pages are unaffected: they opt out of interactive routing entirely, so
        they take the null/static branch before the path check matters.
    *@
    IComponentRenderMode? PageRenderMode =>
        !HttpContext.AcceptsInteractiveRouting() ? null :
        HttpContext.Request.Path.StartsWithSegments("/Account") ? InteractiveServer :
        InteractiveAuto;
}
